course: dictionary
lesson: 8873
title: A shortlist is a small list of the best
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shortlist is a small list of the best people or things, chosen from a bigger group. The final winner is picked from the shortlist. «Parents often make a shortlist of names, and the name must be registered officially within a few weeks of the birth.» Here, the parents first think of many names, then choose a few of the best to think about more closely.
explain: Shortlist can also be a verb. To shortlist someone is to put them on that list. Books, poems, jobs and competitions often use this word. When a book is shortlisted for an award, it is close to winning, but it has not won yet.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Words like best, chosen, final and award tell you that a shortlist is a stage before the winner. Useful phrases are «on the shortlist», «make the shortlist» and «be shortlisted for».
fact: A shortlist is a small list of the best people or things, chosen from a bigger group.
fact: «Shortlist» can be a noun («a shortlist») or a verb («to shortlist»).
fact: «Shortlisted» means put on the shortlist, but not yet the winner.
fact: «On the shortlist» means still in the running for the final choice.
fact: Use the clue words best, chosen, final and award to check what a shortlist is.
exercise: «Parents often make a shortlist of names, and the name must be registered officially within a few weeks of the birth.» What is a shortlist here? | A list of every name in the world | *A small list of the best names, chosen from many | A rule about how long names take | A birth certificate
exercise: «Her poem was shortlisted for the school competition.» What does shortlisted mean? | Crossed out and thrown away | Declared the winner | Read aloud by the teacher | *Put on a small list of the best, but not yet the winner
exercise: Which phrase means a book is still in the running for the final choice? | *on the shortlist | put in the bin | lost in the post | closed for good
test:
Maya says shortlisted means she won the competition. Is she right? | *No, it means chosen among the best, but the winner is not yet picked | Yes, shortlisted means winner | No, it means she lost | Yes, because it has a list in it
«Twelve singers were shortlisted for the show, and three will sing in the final.» How many singers are still in the running for the final? | Twelve, because all of them won | Nine, because nine were cut from the list | *Twelve, because they are all on the shortlist and have not lost yet | Three, but only after the final
exam:
Which sentence uses shortlist as a verb? | «The shortlist was pinned on the classroom board.» | «She read the shortlist of names.» | *«The judges shortlisted six designs from forty entries.» | «The shortlist was very long this year.»
